<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gabrio Casati</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1798–1873</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gabrio Casati was mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> who headed the provisional government formed after the Five Days of Milan drove out the Austrians in March 1848. He favoured union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a> with Charles Albert's Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>. After the Austrian return he went into exile, and later served as a minister and senator, giving his name to the Casati education law of 1859.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gabrio-casati.jpg" alt="Gabrio Casati" width="174" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gabrio_Casati.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
